  "training": {
    "hints": [
      "Translate the lesson into explicit state and permissive logic: Only one road receives a green command at a time, and both roads stop on a fault.",
      "Inputs are simulator feedback (controller_ready, road_a_clear, road_b_clear); PLC logic owns road_a_green, road_b_green.",
      "The loaded ladder also owns road_a_red, road_a_amber, road_b_red and road_b_amber. Each lamp shows its actual command, including conflicting colors; test the interlocks in your ladder.",
      "Test the initial state, the valid condition, and at least one missing permissive.",
      "Load the explicit original traffic reference to alternate the six lamps; the default exercise stays empty. Timing presets 6 s green / 1 s amber / minimum 1 s all-red are educational assumptions, not road engineering.",
      "QUEUE A / B introduces one 50%-scale vehicle per lane. Initial hidden vehicles do not block the crossing. crossing_clear is derived from the conservative delivered-car footprint; manual CLEAR remains an independent entry fixture.",
      "A committed vehicle clears under amber/red or entry-fixture loss. Application Stop freezes plant time. Opposing green commands remain visibly diagnosable and inhibit new entries; occupied all-red delays the next release.",
      "Cart antennas illustrate the shared command source only. No measured radio synchronization or link-health signal is claimed."
    ],
    "solution": {
      "summary": "This is an original functional reference for the control concept, not a copy of the photographed solution.",
      "steps": [
        "Require the documented inputs: controller_ready, road_a_clear, road_b_clear.",
        "Command the documented outputs: road_a_green, road_b_green.",
        "Remove PLC commands when the permissive is lost."
      ],
      "acceptance": "Only one road receives a green command at a time, and both roads stop on a fault."
    },
    "assetRequirements": [
      "mobile traffic signal head",
      "roadway module",
      "signal synchronization link"
    ],
    "machineGuide": {
      "purpose": "Two synchronized mobile signal heads coordinate a safe alternating vehicle-flow state.",
      "startConditions": [
        "The common PLC/watchdog foundation is healthy.",
        "All required simulator inputs are at their documented initial state."
      ],
      "normalSequence": [
        "Load the explicit training reference, enable READY and both manual CLEAR fixtures, then queue A and B.",
        "One-second startup all-red precedes A green; 6 s green, 1 s amber and minimum 1 s all-red alternate the direction.",
        "Keep all-red until crossing_clear. Retain departed vehicles visibly; use QUEUE to explicitly reintroduce a completed vehicle."
      ],
      "stopBehavior": [
        "Entry-fixture loss removes permissive signal commands and restarts all-red; a committed vehicle continues clearing on accepted plant time.",
        "Application Stop clears PLC commands and holds vehicle poses. Run restarts all-red; Reset hides vehicles, clears requests and returns stopped."
      ],
      "faultBehavior": [
        "A missing or stale input must fail safe and remain diagnosable."
      ],
      "expectedObservations": [
        "Only one road receives a green command at a time, and both roads stop on a fault.",
        "Actual occupancy and crossing_clear follow vehicle footprints, not PLC output echoes.",
        "No opposing vehicle entry while the other vehicle route remains committed. Both red on entry-fixture fault while scanning the explicit reference."
      ]
    },
    "sequenceNumber": 68,
